---
description: Core conventions of the Local AI Dev Orchestrator (always on)
globs:
alwaysApply: true
---

- Node 22. The running app keeps **zero npm dependencies** (`node:sqlite`, `node:test`, global `fetch`) and the dashboard stays plain ES modules with no JS bundler. The only package is the Tailwind CLI devDependency: edit `public/css/input.css`, run `npm run css`, and commit `public/style.css`. Do not add any other package.
- Never read, print or commit `.env*`, keys or the live data (`data/`, port 4310). Tests and one-off scripts use random ports, temp dirs and an explicit `ORCH_DB`; `config.js` refuses to hand out the real DB to anything but `node server.js`.
- Plan first (a short written plan, then wait for approval) for architectural changes, schema/DB migrations, new endpoints families and anything touching git/fs safety.
- Never claim a test, build or CI result you did not run. Report real counts: `CI=1 node --test --test-concurrency=4 "test/**/*.test.js"` and the same without `CI=1`.
- Commit identity: this repo has NO local git identity on purpose and the global one must not be used. Commit with
  `GIT_AUTHOR_NAME="Omkar Arote" GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL="OmkarArote@users.noreply.github.com" GIT_COMMITTER_NAME="Omkar Arote" GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL="OmkarArote@users.noreply.github.com" git commit ...`; never `git config user.*`, never force-push; push with `git push origin main`.
- The orchestrator never writes to a service's default branch on its own: task output and its own commits (`.ai/` export, Cursor rules) go to a new branch (throw-away worktree) and reach the default branch only through the human `approve-merge` (`mergeTask` in `lib/git-ops.js`).
- Details: see the other rules (`guards`, `tests`, `ui`) - they load by file type.
